<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/3rd-century-bce">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Campaign</p><h1 class="enc-title">Anabasis of Antiochus III</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">212–205 BCE</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anabasis">Anabasis</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antiochus-iii-the-great">Antiochus III</a> was the great eastern campaign of the Seleucid king Antiochus III from 212 to 205 BCE. He marched through <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/armenia">Armenia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/parthia">Parthia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bactria">Bactria</a> and reached the borders of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, reasserting Seleucid authority over rulers who had broken away. The campaign earned him the title 'the Great', although many of the gains proved temporary.</p></div>
